SynAPSE bundles JAX/Flax NNX ports of third-party code. Everything below is MIT
licensed, same as SynAPSE itself, but the MIT terms require each copyright
notice to travel with the code — so they are recorded here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SynthRL
    https://github.com/argaaw/SynthRL
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Wonchul Shin

    Ported in:
        src/synapse/backbones/synthrl.py
        src/synapse/backbones/synthrl_layers.py
        src/synapse/pretrained/synthrl.py
        src/synapse/pretrained/synthrl_download.py

    The upstream README licenses the released model checkpoints under MIT as
    well, so the weights that `synthrl_download.py` fetches carry the same terms
    as the code.

    Reference:
        Shin, W., & Lee, K. (2025). Cross-domain Synthesizer Sound Matching via
        Reinforcement Learning. In Proceedings of the International Joint
        Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI).

